{
  "$schema": "https://json.schemastore.org/sarif-2.1.0.json",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "runs": [
    {
      "tool": {
        "driver": {
          "name": "equip-sw-lint",
          "semanticVersion": "1.0.0",
          "informationUri": "https://github.com/mhbae-semi-lab/equip-sw-lint",
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "ESL001",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "32-bit tick counter wraps after 24.9 days"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Equipment PCs run for weeks. A deadline 'TickCount + timeout' or a comparison 'TickCount > deadline' flips sign at the wrap: timeouts fire at once or never, watchdogs stop, and the bug appears only after ~25 days in the field."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use Environment.TickCount64 (.NET Core 3.0+) or Stopwatch.GetTimestamp/Elapsed. If you must keep int ticks, only compare differences: unchecked(Environment.TickCount - start) > timeout."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL001",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "Time",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL001_DeadlineBreaksAtWrap"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL002",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Interval measured with the wall clock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Equipment PCs sync their clock with the host/MES or NTP. A jump of minutes makes 'DateTime.Now - start' negative (timeout never fires) or huge (instant timeout alarm), and DST changes do the same with local time."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Measure with Stopwatch.StartNew()/Elapsed or Environment.TickCount64 differences. Keep DateTime.Now for timestamps shown to people and for file retention dates."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL002",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "Time",
                "overlap": "SonarQube S6561",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL002_ClockJumpBreaksTimeout"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL003",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Periodic timer callback can overlap itself"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "System.Threading.Timer and System.Timers.Timer (AutoReset) run callbacks on the thread pool. When a serial query or file write takes longer than the period, a second callback starts on another thread: two threads talk to the same port, replies get mixed, and the pool fills up until the whole program stalls."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Create the timer one-shot (period Timeout.Infinite / AutoReset = false) and re-arm it in a finally block at the end of the callback, or guard with 'if (Interlocked.Exchange(ref _busy, 1) == 1) return;' ... 'finally { _busy = 0; }'."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL003",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL003_SlowCallbackOverlaps"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL004",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Serial/socket read with no timeout"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "SerialPort.ReadTimeout, Socket.ReceiveTimeout and NetworkStream.ReadTimeout default to infinite, and timeouts never apply to ReadAsync. A cable pull, a controller reboot or a half-open TCP link leaves the reading thread stuck with no alarm; the sequence waits forever."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Set port.ReadTimeout / client.ReceiveTimeout (ms) and handle TimeoutException/IOException as a communication alarm. For async reads pass a token from 'new CancellationTokenSource(timeout)'."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL004",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "IO",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL004_SilentDeviceHangsRead"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL005",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Wait with no timeout"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "WaitOne(), Join(), Monitor.Wait(), SemaphoreSlim.Wait() and Process.WaitForExit() with no timeout turn one lost signal into a frozen sequence or a program that never exits on shutdown. Task.Wait/.Result are left to VSTHRD002 / CA rules."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use the timeout overload (WaitOne(ms), Join(ms), Wait(ms)) and raise an alarm or retry when it returns false."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL005",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "shadow",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL005_LostSignalBlocksForever"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL006",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Settings/recipe file overwritten in place"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "File.WriteAllText, StreamWriter(path), FileMode.Create and XDocument.Save(path) truncate the file first and write it afterwards. Equipment is powered off at the switch and programs are killed by watchdogs, so a half-written recipe or config is a real failure: the tool will not start, or starts with defaults."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Write to 'path + \".tmp\"' (same folder), flush (FileStream.Flush(true)), then File.Replace(tmp, path, backup) or File.Move(tmp, path, overwrite: true)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL006",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "shadow",
                "category": "IO",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL006_CrashMidWriteCorruptsRecipe"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL007",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Buffer shared by callback and UI without a lock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Camera/grabber callbacks fill image buffers on their own thread while the UI paints from the same array or Bitmap. Without a lock the screen shows two frames mixed, and a buffer replaced mid-read throws IndexOutOfRange or 'object is in use elsewhere' and takes the vision program down."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Take the same lock in the callback and in the UI, or build the frame in a private buffer and publish it with Interlocked.Exchange (double buffering)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL007",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "shadow",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "PVS-Studio V3223, Infer# RacerD (general data races)",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL007_TornFrameWithoutLock"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL008",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Queue fed by a callback has no size limit"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A frame queue that grows by 1% of the frame rate looks fine in a 10-minute test and runs out of memory after a day. ConcurrentQueue, Queue, BlockingCollection without capacity and unbounded channels never push back on the producer."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Use new BlockingCollection<T>(capacity) with TryAdd (drop and count), Channel.CreateBounded with BoundedChannelFullMode.DropOldest, or check Count before Enqueue and record dropped frames."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL008",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "Memory",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL008_SlowConsumerGrowsQueue"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL009",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Synchronous UI call while holding a lock"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Control.Invoke, Dispatcher.Invoke and SendMessage block until the UI thread runs the call. If the UI thread is waiting for the same lock (a paint or button handler reading shared state), neither side moves: the classic window-message deadlock behind many 'Vision Down' reports."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Inside the lock only copy what the UI needs; after the lock, call BeginInvoke/InvokeAsync (or Dispatcher.BeginInvoke) with the copy."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL009",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "warning"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "enforce",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "Klocwork CS.BANNED.INVOKE (bans all synchronous Control.Invoke)",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL009_InvokeUnderLockDeadlocks"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL010",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Field initialized after receiving already started"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Opening a port, starting a thread or a timer begins delivering callbacks immediately. When the queue or state they use is assigned a line later, a restart that happens to receive the first message early drops it or throws NullReferenceException: a race that shows up as 'sometimes stuck after restart'."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Move the assignment above the Open/Start call (create queues, buffers and state first, start receiving last)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL010",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "shadow",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL010_EarlyMessageLostOnRestart"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ESL011",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "Polling loop with no deadline"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "'while (!axis.IsDone) Thread.Sleep(10);' is fine until a sensor cable breaks or an interlock blocks the motion. Then the sequence never ends, no alarm is raised and the operator only sees a frozen screen."
              },
              "help": {
                "text": "Track elapsed time (var sw = Stopwatch.StartNew(); while (!done && sw.ElapsedMilliseconds < timeout)) and raise a timeout alarm when the loop ends without the state."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://mhbae-semi-lab.github.io/equip-sw-lint/viewer/#rule/ESL011",
              "defaultConfiguration": {
                "level": "note"
              },
              "properties": {
                "stage": "shadow",
                "category": "Threading",
                "overlap": "PVS-Studio V3120/V3032 (related, not the same)",
                "repro": "Repro_ESL011_StuckSensorHangsSequence"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
